WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
A café in Paris.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.180
Your friend checks her wallet and says:

3
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.430
«Je n'ai que dix euros».

4
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.410
You catch the word «ne».

5
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.100
And you know «ne» usually means 'not'.

6
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.090
So does she have ten euros,

7
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.070
or not? Can you order the croissants?

8
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.290
French has more surprises waiting,

9
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.650
like «pas encore» and «aucun».

10
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.030
So how can a French
sentence with «ne» in it

11
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.640
mean 'only' instead of 'not'?

12
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.310
In this mission, you'll shine
a spotlight on the words

13
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.820
that change the meaning.

14
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.020
Then you'll play front or
back with two tricky words,

15
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.950
and unlock six keys.

16
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: crack the code
that turns 'not' into 'only'.
